  "behavior": [
    "Business timezone and current mode state come from authorized stored configuration. Uninitialized modes are null; a recovery pause has no writable epoch. No browser timezone or fabricated initialization is substituted.",
    "Separate accepted-agreement booking context exposes current complete allocation plans and real vehicle versions. Multiple visits preserve exact money, remaining unassigned scope and stable complimentary identities. Historical initial-acceptance commercial packets remain unchanged; accepted quote replacement remains rejected.",
    "Job resources bind retained customer/vehicle/encounter/scope snapshots to the saved head. A private STABLE invoker helper shares the single SQL statement snapshot. Interactive repeatable-read remains rejected by fresh authorization; ordinary read-committed reads see later committed changes. Export snapshot rules are unchanged.",
    "The global pending-change queue is independent of the confirmed calendar window, paginates by creation timestamp and appointment ID, and removes superseded/withdrawn/cancelled proposals without resurrecting them.",
    "The actual typed browser client calls explicit private routes through a disposable real HTTP server and genuine password/TOTP session. It books once, loses the acknowledged response, retains opaque pending identity, retrieves the exact original receipt, explicitly repeats the same operation without creating another job, then proposes/confirms/proposes/withdraws/cancels and retrieves all six history events.",
    "Workspace, agreement, resources, calendar, pending changes, job/history, mode history/save and original lookup use existing origin/cookie/CSRF/admission/fresh provider/local authorization. Unexpected fields, nested duplicates, cross-origin/CSRF failures, paused writes and signed-out reads are rejected. No new raw web-table or financial authority is introduced."
  ],
  "regressions": [
    {
      "cause": "The native journey imported a bundler-only generic pending controller whose existing extensionless module imports are unsupported by the native runner.",
      "fix": "Exercise the real per-domain transport and opaque store directly in the native journey; generic recovery dispatch remains separately unit-tested. No application import-framework rewrite."
    },
    {
      "cause": "The genuine Auth fixture correctly stores America/Indiana/Indianapolis, while the first test incorrectly expected UTC.",
      "fix": "Assert the genuine stored business timezone. The independent SQL fixture still verifies its actual UTC configuration."
    },
    {
      "cause": "An initial context test assumed interactive repeatable-read was permitted, contrary to the existing fresh-authorization fence.",
      "fix": "Assert that repeatable-read is rejected and verify current contexts under ordinary read-committed isolation. Preserve the fence."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native client/HTTP proof is not a rendered browser, React-controller, deployed TLS or physical-device walkthrough. No new scheduling UI or preview delivery is claimed.",
    "Complete included-domain actor/operation/audit/commercial source closure, legacy49 recovery binding, reviewed schema50 registration and runtime composition remain integration dependencies.",
    "Full public current-source release checks and four-width browser acceptance remain before preview adoption. No acceptance is transferred from accepted49.",
    "Accepted amendments, field/custody/photos/completion, remaining finance, complete owner portability/recovery and Google Calendar remain approved unfinished V1 work. No real-data or finance activation."
